# GPU/Slurm environment. Exact torch/vllm pins are DEFERRED until the cluster
# CUDA version is known — see requirements/README.md. Placeholders are ranges,
# NOT verified pins. Do not treat as reproducible until locked.
-r login.in
# PINNED 2026-09-25 against the BITS CSIS driver (570.158.01 = CUDA 12.8).
# CUDA 13 wheels need a 580+ driver, so cu12x is mandatory here.
#
# vLLM's torch pin does NOT track its own CUDA linkage. 0.20.2-0.26.0 pin
# torch==2.11.0 but their compiled extensions link libcudart.so.13. Read from
# the published wheels' DT_NEEDED strings:
#     vllm <= 0.19.1  -> libcudart.so.12   usable here
#     vllm >= 0.20.2  -> libcudart.so.13   needs driver 580+
# 0.19.1 is the newest CUDA 12 release that does not also require
# transformers<5 (0.17.0-0.19.0 do), so it is the only one that leaves the
# installed transformers 5.x alone. It pins torch 2.10.0.
#
# Install with scripts/cluster/fix_torch_cuda.sh (login node only).
torch==2.10.0             # +cu128 build
torchvision==0.25.0       # +cu128 build
torchaudio==2.10.0        # +cu128 build
vllm==0.19.1              # last release linking libcudart.so.12
transformers>=4.44         # >=4.42 required for Gemma-2; 4.44+ safer
tokenizers>=0.19
accelerate>=0.33
huggingface_hub>=0.24
sentencepiece>=0.2
protobuf>=4.25
safetensors>=0.4
